Video

An Expo-powered cross‑platform app that showcases location‑based services, Google Places integration, and real‑time user interactions.

✨ Features
Cross‑platform: Runs on Android, iOS, and web via Expo.
Location & Places: Uses expo-location and Google Places API to fetch nearby venues.
Authentication: Integrated with expo-auth-session for social sign‑in.
Real‑time UI: Animated maps with clustering via react-native-map-clustering.
State‑of‑the‑art UI: Lottie animations, custom icons, and dark/light themes.
🛠️ Tech Stack
Layer	Technology
Framework	Expo SDK 54 (React Native)
Language	TypeScript
Navigation	expo-router & @react-navigation
State Management	React hooks
Styling	Tailwind‑like utilities via expo-style (custom)
Backend	Firebase (auth, Firestore)
Maps	react-native-maps, react-native-map-clustering
Location	expo-location, expo-crypto
Testing	Expo CLI built‑in lint & TypeScript checks
📦 Installation
bash

npm install

npm start

🔧 Configuration
Environment variables: Create a .env file at the project root with Firebase credentials and Google Places API key. Example:
env

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_key_here
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=your_key_here
Expo settings: Adjust app.json for custom splash screens, icons, and update URLs.
